SUMMARY:📢 Post #5: Video / Reel Script & Teardown — DNS Infrastructure & Deliverability
DESCRIPTION:LINKEDIN SCHEDULED POST: POST #5 (Day 11)\nFORMAT: Video / Reel Script & Teardown\nTOPIC: DNS Infrastructure & Deliverability\nATTACHED ASSET: Video Script: outputs/linkedin_content/reels_and_video_scripts/reels_and_video_scripts.md (#2)\nTARGET GOAL: Record 50s selfie video following Script #2, or post as high-engagement text post.\n\nREADY-TO-PASTE COPY:\n-----------------------------------------\nWhy your $12\,000 commercial equipment quotes are ending up in your client's spam folder (and how to fix it in 2 hours).\n\nYou send a detailed commercial proposal or invoice from your CRM or Microsoft 365 / Google Workspace. Three days later\, the client says: "I never got it."\n\nWhen we audit contractor IT infrastructure\, 7 out of 10 times we find an unauthenticated legacy SPF record or missing DMARC enforcement.\n\nIf your domain's SPF record has a neutral "?all" mechanism or omits your active CRM sending IP\, modern inbox filters (Gmail\, Outlook) automatically quarantine your emails.\n\nThe financial fallout:\n• Delayed payment cycles\n• Lost commercial proposals\n• Customer payment disputes\n\nFixing your DNS records (SPF\, DKIM\, DMARC p=quarantine) takes less than 120 minutes and restores 99.8%+ inbox deliverability.\n\nDon't let DNS misconfigurations silently choke your cash flow.\n\n#EmailDeliverability #ITInfrastructure #BusinessSystems #CyberSecurity\n-----------------------------------------\n\nPOSTING INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Copy the text above.\n2. Attach the local file if required.\n3. Publish to LinkedIn at 09:00 AM!
LOCATION:LinkedIn (https://www.linkedin.com)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Time to publish LinkedIn Post #5 in 15 minutes!
