SUMMARY:📢 Post #6: Contrarian Metric Analysis — KPI Rigor & Unit Economics
DESCRIPTION:LINKEDIN SCHEDULED POST: POST #6 (Day 14)\nFORMAT: Contrarian Metric Analysis\nTOPIC: KPI Rigor & Unit Economics\nATTACHED ASSET: Text Only\nTARGET GOAL: Provocative management insight prompting founders to rethink operational KPIs.\n\nREADY-TO-PASTE COPY:\n-----------------------------------------\nThe most dangerous metric in trade contracting: 'Revenue per truck' without tracking dispatch response time.\n\nA contractor can boast $350k revenue per van\, but if their dispatch response latency is 45 minutes\, they are burning through $20\,000/mo in paid Google Ads leads just to keep those trucks rolling.\n\nWhen you measure:\n1. First-touch response latency (Target: < 60s)\n2. Off-hours call salvage rate (Target: > 40%)\n3. Digital proposal option adoption (Target: > 55% choosing Tier 2/3)\n\nYour existing fleet generates 25% more gross margin with ZERO additional overhead.\n\nMeasure the handoffs\, not just the tailpipes.\n\n#BusinessMetrics #UnitEconomics #ContractorLeadership #Operations\n-----------------------------------------\n\nPOSTING INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Copy the text above.\n2. Attach the local file if required.\n3. Publish to LinkedIn at 06:30 PM!
LOCATION:LinkedIn (https://www.linkedin.com)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
BEGIN:VALARM
