SUMMARY:📢 Post #9: Reputation Engine Breakdown — Google Map Pack & Review Deficit
DESCRIPTION:LINKEDIN SCHEDULED POST: POST #9 (Day 21)\nFORMAT: Reputation Engine Breakdown\nTOPIC: Google Map Pack & Review Deficit\nATTACHED ASSET: Text Only\nTARGET GOAL: Breaks down the automated SMS review capture engine.\n\nREADY-TO-PASTE COPY:\n-----------------------------------------\nHaving a 4.8-star rating means nothing on Google Maps if you only have 28 reviews.\n\nIn trade contracting\, the Google Local Map Pack captures over 70% of high-intent mobile search clicks.\n\nWhen a regional market leader holds 4\,500+ reviews and your business holds under 300\, Google's local algorithm surrenders the top 3 placements to your competitor—even if your field craftsmanship is vastly superior.\n\nWhy do established contractors have so few reviews?\n\nBecause they rely on field technicians remembering to ask: "Hey\, could you leave us a review?"\n\nTechnicians are focused on fixing pipes and compressors\, not asking for reviews.\n\nThe automated solution:\nConnect CRM job completion webhooks to trigger an automated SMS review request exactly 45 minutes after the technician marks the job complete.\n\nClients who install this review capture engine systematically generate 15–25 verified 5-star reviews every single month on autopilot.\n\nTake human memory out of your reputation engine.\n\n#LocalSEO #GoogleMaps #ContractorMarketing #ReputationManagement\n-----------------------------------------\n\nPOSTING INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Copy the text above.\n2. Attach the local file if required.\n3. Publish to LinkedIn at 06:30 PM!
LOCATION:LinkedIn (https://www.linkedin.com)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
