SUMMARY:📢 Post #15: Systems Philosophy — Software vs Workflows
DESCRIPTION:LINKEDIN SCHEDULED POST: POST #15 (Day 35)\nFORMAT: Systems Philosophy\nTOPIC: Software vs Workflows\nATTACHED ASSET: Text Only\nTARGET GOAL: Addresses software bloat in mid-market service firms.\n\nREADY-TO-PASTE COPY:\n-----------------------------------------\nBuying more SaaS tools won't fix a broken operational workflow.\n\nContractors love buying software. They have ServiceTitan\, Jobber\, Housecall Pro\, Zapier\, HubSpot\, Mailchimp\, and three different messaging widgets.\n\nYet their office staff still spends 15 hours a week re-typing customer addresses\, copy-pasting dispatch notes\, and manually texting technicians.\n\nWhy?\n\nBecause software is not a workflow.\n\nA tool is just a database. A workflow is the automated bridge connecting:\n• When Job Signs Off -> Trigger Review SMS\n• When Invoice Exceeds $3\,000 -> Trigger Warranty Follow-up\n• When Single-Trade Customer Is Tagged -> Schedule Cross-Sell Offer\n\nBefore you buy another $300/month software subscription\, map out the handoffs between the tools you already own.\n\n#SaaS #OperationsArchitecture #WorkflowAutomation #FieldService\n-----------------------------------------\n\nPOSTING INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Copy the text above.\n2. Attach the local file if required.\n3. Publish to LinkedIn at 06:30 PM!
LOCATION:LinkedIn (https://www.linkedin.com)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
